cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use SAUT, or build on the concepts it implements — cross-harness
  privilege semantics for agent skills, the always-on/on-invoke cost
  passport, and trigger/obedience measurement across harnesses — please
  cite it as below.
title: "SAUT — Skill Assurance Under Trust"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Yuriy
    family-names: Orlov
    email: yuriy.orlov@undertrust.dev
abstract: >-
  SAUT is an assurance tool for AI-agent skills. It reads a skill or
  subagent authored to the Agent Skills format and reports what no single
  harness will tell you: per harness, whether the declared tool allowlist
  is a restriction, a pre-approval grant, informational prose or a field
  dropped on render; what the artifact costs in every session versus on
  invocation; and — by compiling it into a scratch workspace and running
  each harness headlessly — whether the harness actually fires it and
  whether the run stays inside the declaration it made. The recorded
  semantics is data with provenance, and the bench measures it rather
  than asserting it.
keywords:
  - ai-agents
  - agentic-coding
  - agent-skills
  - skill-assurance
  - static-analysis
  - evaluation
  - token-budget
  - least-privilege
  - claude-code
  - codex
  - opencode
repository-code: "https://github.com/yurgeno/saut"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.6.0
date-released: '2026-09-03'
